t=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NY_State_Area_Command_SSI.svg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=3738333","sha1":"dfa035d7203fd270447bfc31eb3ae8bb838469ea","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2008-03-19 16:00:33","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"NY State Area Command SSI","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"With insignia|PD US Army USAIOH|Unchecked SVG validity|Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (SSI) of the Army National Guard|Heraldry of the US Army Elements, Joint Force Headquarters|New York Army National Guard Heraldry|53rd Troop Command","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoulder_Sleeve_Insignia_(US_Army)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (US Army)\">Shoulder Sleeve Insignia</a> of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Army_National_Guard\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:New York Army National Guard\">New York Army National Guard</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/53rd_Troop_Command_(United_States)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:53rd Troop Command (United States)\">53rd Troop Command</a> (New York State Area Command).\n</p>\n<dl><dt>Description</dt></dl>\n<ul><li><i>On an ultramarine blue trapezoid with a 1/8 inch (.32 cm) scarlet border, 3 1/4 inches (8.26 cm) in height and 2 1/2 inches (6.35 cm) in width overall, a scarlet sword surmounted by a stylized yellow crown of seven points.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dt>Symbolism</dt></dl>\n<ul><li>New York State is represented by the crown, recalling the crown on the Statue of Liberty, symbol of the city and state, which emphasizes the traditional freedoms long associated with New York. The sword represents the National Guard and denotes readiness. Blue refers to the many waterways and natural water resources of New York and is taken from the state flag. Red reflects courage; gold is for excellence.</li></ul>\n<dl><dt>Background</dt></dl>\n<ul><li>The shoulder sleeve insignia was authorized for Headquarters, State Area Command, New York Army National Guard on 18 February 1994.</li></ul>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2008-03-19","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"Own work, after <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NY_State_Area_Command_SSI.png\" title=\"File:NY State Area Command SSI.png\">Image:NY State Area Command SSI.png</a>.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Fvasconcellos\" title=\"User:Fvasconcellos\">Fvasconcellos</a> (<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Fvasconcellos\" title=\"User talk:Fvasconcellos\">talk</a><span style=\"white-space:nowrap\"> <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">·</span></span> <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Contributions/Fvasconcellos\" title=\"Special:Contributions/Fvasconcellos\">contribs</a>)","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"<i>This image shows a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/flag\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:flag\">flag</a>, a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/coat_of_arms\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:coat of arms\">coat of arms</a>, a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/seal_(device)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:seal (device)\">seal</a> or some other official <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/insignia\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:insignia\">insignia</a></b> produced by the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Army_Institute_of_Heraldry\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:United States Army Institute of Heraldry\">United States Army Institute of Heraldry</a></b>.  It is in the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/public_domain\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:public domain\">public domain</a></b> but its use is restricted by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/pkg/USCODE-2010-title18/pdf/USCODE-2010-title18-partI-chap33-sec704.pdf\">Title 18, United States Code, Section 704</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/18/704\">[1]</a> and the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/granule/CFR-2012-title32-vol3/CFR-2012-title32-vol3-part507/content-detail.html\">Code of Federal Regulations (32 CFR, Part 507)</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.ecfr.gov/cgi-bin/text-idx?mc=true&amp;node=pt32.3.507&amp;rgn=div5\">[2]</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/32/part-507\">[3]</a>.  Permission to use these images in the USA for most commercial purposes must be obtained from The Institute of Heraldry prior to their use.</i>","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"insignia","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/svg+xml"}],"revisions":[{"revid":1015469636,"parentid":912908863,"timestamp":"2025-03-31T07:28:16Z","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{validSVG}}\n{{Information\n|Description=[[:w:Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (US Army)|Shoulder Sleeve Insignia]] of the {{w|New York Army National Guard}} [[:w:53rd Troop Command (United States)|53rd Troop Command]] (New York State Area Command).\n;Description\n*''On an ultramarine blue trapezoid with a 1/8 inch (.32 cm) scarlet border, 3 1/4 inches (8.26 cm) in height and 2 1/2 inches (6.35 cm) in width overall, a scarlet sword surmounted by a stylized yellow crown of seven points.''\n;Symbolism\n*New York State is represented by the crown, recalling the crown on the Statue of Liberty, symbol of the city and state, which emphasizes the traditional freedoms long associated with New York. The sword represents the National Guard and denotes readiness. Blue refers to the many waterways and natural water resources of New York and is taken from the state flag. Red reflects courage; gold is for excellence.\n;Background\n*The shoulder sleeve insignia was authorized for Headquarters, State Area Command, New York Army National Guard on 18 February 1994.\n|Source=Own work, after [[:Image:NY State Area Command SSI.png]].\n|Date=2008-03-19\n|Author={{user|Fvasconcellos}}\n|Permission={{PD-USGov-Military-Army-USAIOH}}\n{{Insignia}}\n}}\n\n[[Category:Heraldry of the US Army Elements, Joint Force Headquarters]]\n[[Category:New York Army National Guard Heraldry]]\n[[Category:Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (SSI) of the Army National Guard]]\n[[Category:53rd Troop Command]]"}}}]},{"pageid":3954024,"ns":6,"title":"File:111EngrBdeSSI.jpg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"timestamp":"2008-04-28T06:45:44Z","user":"Nobunaga24","size":11330,"width":217,"height":313,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/58/111EngrBdeSSI.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":333,"thumbheight":480,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/58/111EngrBdeSSI.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":333,"height":480},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/58/111EngrBdeSSI.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File: